# Instructions for REBUILDING on windows, Jul 08
# NOT necessary for running shipped code as is


1) Get MinGW | Minimalist GNU for Windows
http://www.mingw.org/wiki/Getting_Started
do the "Automated Installer" bits using
https://sourceforge.net/project/showfiles.php?group_id=2435&package_id=240780
install most basic components (but *not* java)
especially: c, c++, f77 compilers, make
Do the default install

2) Get gfortran for windows
http://gcc.gnu.org/wiki/GFortran
Get the "mingw build", or "native Windows" build" see 
http://gcc.gnu.org/wiki/GFortranBinaries
This redirects to something like (as of Jan 2010)
http://quatramaran.ens.fr/~coudert/gfortran/gfortran-windows.exe
Put it in, say
C:/MinGW/gfortran
(website suggests you avoid places with spaces, like "Program Files")

3) Get a recent jdk (*NOT the jre*) from sun, e.g. browse around
http://java.sun.com/javase/downloads/index.jsp

Use at least Java 1.5
Do the standard install.

4) To build native pieces (in DOS)
- add the java area to your path, e.g.
% path C:/Program\ Files/Java/jdk1.6.0_10/bin
do this somehow permanently too (autoexec.bat?)
so, e.g. 
% java -version
produces sane output

You need to set environment variables 
(On WinXP: tunnel down from: Start/My Computer/View System Information/Advanced-Tab/Environment Variables)

% set CSIRO_OSTYPE=cygwin
% set SEISMIC_INVERTER_HOME=root_of distribution (i.e. directory containing au, jars etc)
% add to PATH: SEISMIC_INVERTER_HOME/scripts

then the compile is
% make -f Makefile

5) Running
Make sure your PATH sees
a) the java executables area
b) the scripts directory of the Delivery distribution: ../../../../../scripts/
For a script, see the example ../../../../../scripts/csem1Dinverter
Your Windows environment must have set the variables

SEISMIC_INVERTER_HOME=root_of Delivery distribution (i.e. directory containing au, jars etc)
CSIRO_OSTYPE=cygwin

to run, for example:

% csem1Dinverter -v 2 -h


